---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
---

<Base
  title="Live in Andorra | Moving to Andorra"
  description="If you want to live in Andorra or are moving to Andorra: residency, banks and housing in English, from Govern.ad and the BOPA."
  path="/"
  overlayNav={true}
>
  <section class="hero">
    <div class="hero-content">
      <div class="hero-label">Andorra</div>
      <h1>If you’re thinking of living here</h1>
      <p>
        A small country in the Pyrenees. If you want to live in Andorra
        you need a permit, a bank and a place to sleep. This site puts
        the official pages into English.
      </p>
      <a href="/become-a-resident" class="hero-cta">Become a Resident</a>
      <a href="/directory" class="hero-cta secondary">The directory</a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="why" id="lifestyle">
    <div class="why-header">
      <h2>What you’re actually choosing</h2>
      <p>
        Andorra is a country, not a ski resort with a tax rumour attached.
        Catalan is official. The capital is a short drive from both borders.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="pillars">
      <div class="pillar">
        <h3>A permit, not a vibe</h3>
        <p>
          You live here under Andorran immigration law. The letters that
          matter are the Government’s: A.1, J.1, D.1, B.1.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="pillar">
        <h3>Small, on purpose</h3>
        <p>
          Seven parishes. One public hospital. Three banking groups. You
          will see the same streets in winter and in August.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="pillar">
        <h3>Mountains, then paperwork</h3>
        <p>
          Ski valleys and high villages are close. So are immigration,
          notaries and the Comú. That is the point of the place.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="pillar">
        <h3>Read the live text</h3>
        <p>
          Fees and quotas move. Start with
          <a href="https://www.govern.ad/" target="_blank" rel="noopener"
            >Govern.ad</a
          >
          and the BOPA, then talk to counsel.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="life" id="living">
    <div class="life-header">
      <h2>The year, without the brochure</h2>
      <p>
        Winter is busy on the eastern and western ski roads. Summer is
        quieter. Most people who stay care more about the middle of the
        week than about a powder morning.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="life-grid">
      <div class="life-card">
        <div class="life-label">Winter</div>
        <h3>Grandvalira and Pal-Arinsal</h3>
        <p>
          The slopes sit next to the villages. You are not transferring
          two hours from a city airport. Roads still ice. Plan for that.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="life-card">
        <div class="life-label">Summer</div>
        <h3>Trails and a shorter street</h3>
        <p>
          High paths, Sorteny, Comapedrosa, the Madriu valley. Shops and
          restaurants stay open. The capital does not empty.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="life-card">
        <div class="life-label">Everyday</div>
        <h3>Appointments and errands</h3>
        <p>
          Banks, schools and immigration sit in the central valley. If
          you live higher up, you drive. That is a choice, not a flaw.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <a href="/living-in-andorra" class="text-link">Daily life</a>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="section-header">
      <h2>Start here</h2>
      <p>
        Permits, named firms, the seven parishes, and how we will list
        homes. No invented houses. No invented fees.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="card-grid">
      <div class="card">
        <div class="card-label">Residency</div>
        <h3>Become a resident</h3>
        <p>
          Official permit types, Law 2/2026 figures from the BOPA, and
          links to Govern.ad.
        </p>
        <a href="/become-a-resident" class="text-link">Read it</a>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <div class="card-label">Directory</div>
        <h3>Named firms</h3>
        <p>
          Banks, counsel, AGIA agents, clinics and a school. Each has
          its own website.
        </p>
        <a href="/directory" class="text-link">Open the directory</a>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <div class="card-label">Parishes</div>
        <h3>Seven communes</h3>
        <p>
          Andorra la Vella to Sant Julià. Pick the parish before you
          pick the house.
        </p>
        <a href="/parishes" class="text-link">The parishes</a>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <div class="card-label">Properties</div>
        <h3>How we list homes</h3>
        <p>
          A template until we have a file we have seen. AGIA-registered
          agents in the meantime.
        </p>
        <a href="/properties" class="text-link">The listing rules</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="life">
    <div class="life-header">
      <h2>If you are actually moving</h2>
      <p>
        Country of departure, a bank meeting, buying before you are
        resident, and the Government’s own D.3 page.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="card-grid">
      <div class="card">
        <div class="card-label">Relocation</div>
        <h3>Moving to Andorra</h3>
        <p>UK, Spain and France. Same Andorran file, different papers.</p>
        <a href="/moving-to-andorra" class="text-link">Start here</a>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <div class="card-label">Banking</div>
        <h3>Open an account</h3>
        <p>KYC in person. AFA supervision. Three named banks.</p>
        <a href="/opening-a-bank-account" class="text-link">The bank note</a>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <div class="card-label">Property</div>
        <h3>Buy as a non-resident</h3>
        <p>Foreign-investment authorisation. Tax at 6% or 10% as published.</p>
        <a href="/buying-property" class="text-link">The purchase rules</a>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <div class="card-label">D.3</div>
        <h3>Digital nomad</h3>
        <p>Remote work, a quota, 90 days. Means “set by regulation”.</p>
        <a href="/digital-nomad" class="text-link">Read D.3</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="section-header">
      <h2>The permits people ask about</h2>
      <p>
        Each note follows a live Govern.ad page. The euro figures that
        appear are from the BOPA or the tariffs table.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="card-grid">
      <div class="card">
        <div class="card-label">D.1</div>
        <h3>Residence without work</h3>
        <p>
          Named subtypes, 90 days on the immigration page, and the
          million-euro investment in Law 2/2026.
        </p>
        <a href="/residence-without-work" class="text-link">Read D.1</a>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <div class="card-label">B.1</div>
        <h3>Family reunification</h3>
        <p>Who the Government lists, and the household means test.</p>
        <a href="/family-reunification" class="text-link">Read B.1</a>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <div class="card-label">Tax</div>
        <h3>Tax residence</h3>
        <p>Article 8 of Law 5/2014. 183 days, or the centre of interests.</p>
        <a href="/tax-residence" class="text-link">Read the tax note</a>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <div class="card-label">J.1 / D.4</div>
        <h3>Work on your own account</h3>
        <p>Self-employed residence and work, and the entrepreneur programme.</p>
        <a href="/self-employed-residence" class="text-link">Read J.1</a>
        &nbsp;·&nbsp;
        <a href="/entrepreneur-residence" class="text-link">Read D.4</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
